<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="46456" href="schedule/2016/spring/MUS/521/46456.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120161" href="schedule/2016/spring.xml">Spring 2016</term><subject id="MUS" href="schedule/2016/spring/MUS.xml">Music</subject><course id="521" href="schedule/2016/spring/MUS/521.xml">Hist Studies in 20thC Music</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>TOPIC: 1964 In this course, we will examine the diverse trends in American music production and performance during the year 1964. Drawing from popular music, film soundtracks, contemporaneous composers and compositions, premieres, new stage productions and revivals, radio and television broadcasts, oral histories, and local archives, the course will offer unique insights into the American soundscape of just over half a century ago.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2016-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2334</roomNumber><buildingName>Music Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Magee" firstName="G">Magee, G</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>